hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2747","Narrated to us by Al-Abbar ibn Al-Ala', Ali ibn Khushram, and Ahmad ibn Mani', who said: Narrated to us Sufyan. Al-Abbar said: I heard him from Abu Az-Zubayr, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Babahah informing from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \O Banu Abd Manaf! Let no one be prevented from circumambulating this House (the Ka'bah)"""
"2748","###\n Narrated to us Abdullah bin Imran Al-Abidi, who narrated to us Sa'id bin Salim Al-Qidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mu'mal, meaning Al-Makhzumi, on the authority of Humaid, the freed slave of Afra', on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Dharr (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \There is no prayer after Fajr (the dawn prayer) and no prayer after Asr (the afternoon prayer"""
"2749","###\n Narrated to us by Sa'id bin Abdullah bin Abd al-Hakam, who said: Narrated to us by Hafsa bin Umar, meaning al-Adani, who said: Narrated to us by Abd al-Jabbar bin al-Ward, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaikah, who said: Al-Miswar bin Makhramah performed Tawaf (circumambulation) of the Ka'bah eighteen circuits. Then, he prayed two rak'ahs for every seven circuits. He said: The Messenger of"
